          "note": "Young's Modulus: a main subheading of 5.3 Stress, strain and Young's modulus, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 96-97."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Young's modulus",
            "text": "The stress applied per unit strain is called Young's modulus"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{i.e.}\\quad Y = \\frac{\\text{Tensile stress}}{\\text{Tensile strain}}",
            "text_alt": "i.e. Y = Tensile stress / Tensile strain"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "Y = \\frac{F/A}{\\Delta L/L_0} \\qquad (5.6)",
            "text_alt": "Y = (F/A) / (ΔL/L₀)   (5.6)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "It has the same unit as that of stress i.e., N m⁻² or Pa. The value of Young's modulus of different material is given in Table 5.1."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "There are various methods to determine the Young's modulus of a wire. One of the method is Searle's method."
          },
          {
